        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Method Resolution Order",
          "items": [
            "Tries `self`, then `&self`, then `&mut self`",
            "Then derefs once and repeats",
            "First match wins"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Not For Inheritance",
          "text": "Deref polymorphism is an anti-pattern: do not use `Deref` to fake a base class between your own structs. It is for pointers."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Drop: Cleanup On Exit"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`fn drop(&mut self)` runs when the value leaves scope",
            "Variables drop in reverse declaration order",
            "Struct fields drop in declaration order",
            "Calling `.drop()` by hand is a compile error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let a = CSP(\"first\");",
            "let b = CSP(\"second\");",
            "drop(a);   // std::mem::drop, frees now",
            "// b drops at scope end — LIFO order"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Rc<T>: Shared Ownership, Single Thread",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Free Early, Or Never",
          "items": [
            "`std::mem::drop(x)` frees before scope end",
            "`std::mem::forget(x)` skips the destructor",
            "`forget` is safe — a leak is not unsound"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Nested Drop Is Recursive",
          "text": "Dropping a `Box<Node>` drops the whole chain behind it. A million-node list can blow the stack on the way out."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Many Owners, One Value",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Rc<T>` = reference counted shared ownership",
            "Freed when the last owner drops",
            "For values where you cannot tell which owner dies last",
            "Hands out immutable access only"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let a = Rc::new(5);",
            "let b = Rc::clone(&a);   // count = 2",
            "println!(\"{}\", Rc::strong_count(&a));",
            "// b drops at scope end, back to 1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Clone Is Not A Copy",
          "items": [
            "`Rc::clone(&a)` bumps a counter — one increment",
            "The payload is never copied",
            "Write `Rc::clone(&a)`, not `a.clone()`",
            "Readers then see a count bump, not a deep copy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Memory Layout"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "struct RcBox<T> {",
            "    strong: Cell<usize>,",
            "    weak: Cell<usize>,",
            "    value: T,",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "strong",
              "weak",
              "value"
            ],
            "indices": true,
