            "highlight": [],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "one heap allocation"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two counters live next to the value",
            "They are plain `Cell<usize>` — non-atomic",
            "Exactly why `Rc<T>` is neither `Send` nor `Sync`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mutating Through An Rc"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Returns",
            "When"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Rc::get_mut`",
              "`Some(&mut T)`",
              "strong 1, weak 0"
            ],
            [
              "`Rc::make_mut`",
              "`&mut T`",
              "clones if shared"
            ],
            [
              "`Rc::ptr_eq`",
              "`bool`",
              "same address"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`&mut` through an `Rc` needs interior mutability",
            "`make_mut` is clone-on-write in one call",
            "`ptr_eq` compares addresses, not values"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "With `Box`, `b` would ==move== `a` — `c` cannot use it",
            "`Rc` lets both lists **own** the same tail",
            "`a` frees only after `b` and `c` both drop"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Rc in Practice: Shared Tails, Counts & Clone-On-Write",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Shared Tail"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let a = Rc::new(Cons(5, Rc::new(Nil)));",
            "let b = Cons(3, Rc::clone(&a));",
            "let c = Cons(4, Rc::clone(&a));",
            "// b and c share tail a — Box cannot"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Watching The Count"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let a = Rc::new(5);",
            "{",
            "    let b = Rc::clone(&a);",
            "    // strong_count(&a) == 2",
            "}   // b dropped here",
            "// strong_count(&a) == 1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Moment",
            "strong_count"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "after `a`",
              "1"
            ],
            [
              "after `b`, `c`",
              "3"
            ],
            [
              "`c` leaves scope",
              "2"
            ],
            [
              "all dropped",
              "0 — **freed**"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Clone-On-Write"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let mut a = Rc::new(vec![1]);",
            "let b = Rc::clone(&a);",
            "Rc::make_mut(&mut a).push(2);",
            "// a = [1, 2] (cloned), b = [1]"
          ],
          "note": "clones only because b shares it"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Rc Or Box?",
          "text": "One owner you can name → `Box`. Several owners and no way to know which dies last → `Rc`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Arc<T>: Shared Ownership Across Threads",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Cost Profile",
          "text": "Clone and drop are O(1) counter updates. You pay one extra pointer hop, two counters of memory, and a check on every drop."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Pitfall Ahead",
          "text": "An `Rc` cycle never reaches zero, so it never frees. Two pages on that is coming."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Atomically Ref Counted",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same API as `Rc<T>`, safe to move between threads",
            "`Arc<T>` is `Send + Sync` when `T: Send + Sync`",
            "`Rc<T>` is neither, by design",
            "`Arc` alone gives shared reads, not mutability"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let data = Arc::new(vec![1, 2, 3]);",
            "let d = Arc::clone(&data);  // one per thread",
            "thread::spawn(move || println!(\"{:?}\", d));",
            "// then join the handle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "The Error You Will See",
          "items": [
            "\"`Rc<...>` cannot be sent between threads safely\"",
            "Raised by the `Send` bound on `thread::spawn`",
            "Swap in `Arc` — ergonomics are identical"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Inside The Counter"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Counters are `AtomicUsize`, not `Cell`",
            "Increments use `Ordering::Relaxed`",
            "Final decrement is `Release`, then an `Acquire` fence",
            "The fence makes the drop see every prior write"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Op",
            "`Rc`",
            "`Arc`"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "clone",
              "plain add",
              "atomic RMW"
            ],
            [
              "cost",
              "~1 cycle",
              "10-30x contended"
            ],
            [
              "threads",
              "one",
              "many"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The cost is cache-line ownership transfer",
            "Default to `Rc` inside a single thread",
            "Pay for `Arc` only when the value crosses threads"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Classic Shape"
        },
