    {
      "page_title": "Interior Mutability: Cell and RefCell",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Handles And Unwrapping",
          "items": [
            "`Arc::strong_count` is a racy snapshot only",
            "`Arc::try_unwrap(a)` gives `Ok(T)` if last handle",
            "Otherwise `Err(a)` hands the `Arc` back"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "No Lock Needed",
          "text": "For immutable shared data — a config, a lookup table — `Arc<T>` on its own is enough. Lock only what actually mutates."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Atomics Are Not A Cure",
          "text": "`Arc` cycles leak exactly like `Rc` cycles. Atomics fix data races, not the topology of your graph."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mutate Through &T",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Interior mutability: mutate data behind an immutable ref",
            "Legal only because `UnsafeCell` sits inside",
            "`UnsafeCell<T>` is the one legal `&T` to `&mut T`",
            "Every cell type in std is built on it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Moved, Not Removed",
          "text": "The borrow rule is not deleted. `RefCell` enforces the same rule at runtime instead of at compile time."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cell: Whole Values Only"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hands out no references at all",
            "`get()` needs `Copy`; plus `set()`, `replace()`, `take()`",
            "Zero runtime overhead and it can never panic",
            "Right size for counters and flags"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let c = Cell::new(0u32);",
            "c.set(c.get() + 1);      // through &self",
            "let old = c.replace(9);  // old = 1",
            "let v = c.take();        // v = 9, cell = 0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "RefCell: Tracked Borrows"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Guard",
            "Flag"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`borrow()`",
              "`Ref<T>`",
              "+1 shared"
            ],
            [
              "`borrow_mut()`",
              "`RefMut<T>`",
              "-1 exclusive"
            ],
            [
              "`try_borrow`",
              "`Result`",
              "no panic"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "matrix",
          "spec": {
            "rows": [
              [
                "0 free",
                "1..n shared"
              ],
              [
                "-1 mutable"
              ]
            ],
